# Debian's system GLib is not ThreadSanitizer-instrumented, so synchronization
# inside its worker pools is invisible to TSan (reports have appeared in both
# g_queue_pop_tail and g_strsplit during SDL startup). CNA and museum frames
# remain instrumented and are not suppressed.
race:libglib-2.0.so
race:libgio-2.0.so
# Mesa's Gallium driver (llvmpipe/radeonsi) is not instrumented either: two reports with only
# libgallium frames appeared in the 2026-10-20 TSan tour of the audio, notification, Inspector and
# network rooms. Museum and CNA frames stay instrumented and unsuppressed.
race:libgallium-*.so
# UBSan's runtime probes memory with pipe() (__sanitizer::IsAccessibleMemoryRange, its vptr checks). In a binary that
# carries both sanitizers (build-tsan with -fsanitize=thread,undefined, 2026-10-25) TSan reports those probes racing with
# each other, 19 times in one audio_check run and every report in that runtime: the libraries' own interplay.
called_from_lib:libubsan.so
